    question_en: "AeroNova Airways operates an online booking and ticketing platform for regional flights. The backend application runs on Amazon EC2 instances and interacts with an Amazon DynamoDB table for flight seat inventory and an Amazon S3 bucket to store electronic boarding passes and receipt PDFs. The platform requires a consistent baseline capacity of 10 EC2 instances running 24 hours a day, 7 days a week throughout the year, with an Auto Scaling group launching additional instances during daytime travel search surges.\n\nDuring an internal security review, the security team discovered that long-lived IAM user access keys are embedded in application configuration files across all EC2 instances to authenticate requests to DynamoDB and S3. Furthermore, the finance department requires reducing compute costs for the continuous baseline workload while maintaining high availability.\n\nWhich combination of actions should a solutions architect recommend to satisfy these requirements MOST cost-effectively and securely?",
