    question_en: "A SaaS company provides a real-time analytics dashboard hosted in the us-east-1 Region. The application consists of a single-page frontend application stored in a private Amazon S3 bucket and dynamic REST API endpoints hosted on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Users in Europe and Asia report high latency when loading the dashboard interface and fetching real-time analytics data. Company security policy mandates that the Amazon S3 bucket must remain strictly private and allow access only through a content delivery network (CDN).\n\nWhich solution will reduce latency for global users and meet the security requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
