    question_en: "A SaaS analytics dashboard vendor is designing an event ingestion and processing pipeline. The platform receives high volumes of metric telemetry events from customer applications. Each incoming event must be processed independently by two separate backend subsystems:\n\n1. A latency-sensitive real-time aggregation engine that continuously updates live customer dashboards.\n2. A cost-sensitive, fault-tolerant batch reporting engine that aggregates long-term historical analytics and can tolerate task interruptions.\n\nThe architecture must decouple event producers from consumers, prevent message loss during sudden traffic spikes, enable both processing tiers to scale independently based on demand, and minimize overall compute costs.\n\nWhich solution should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?",
