    question_en: "A company hosts a web application on Amazon EC2 instances. The application experiences unpredictable traffic fluctuations, causing performance degradation during traffic spikes and unnecessary costs during low-traffic periods. The company requires a solution that is highly available, resilient to the failure of an entire Availability Zone, and able to automatically adjust compute capacity. In addition, the system must automatically detect and replace instances if the application process stops responding to web requests.\n\nWhich solution should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?",
