    question_en: "A fintech company, PayFlow Solutions, runs a high-volume payment processing application on AWS. The application consists of a stateless web tier that validates incoming transactions and a MySQL-compatible relational database that stores merchant accounts and ledger transactions. The system experiences unpredictable traffic spikes during major promotional sales.\n\nA solutions architect must design a highly available architecture that meets the following requirements:\n- The compute tier must automatically scale capacity based on incoming traffic demand while maintaining high availability across multiple Availability Zones.\n- The database tier must support MySQL compatibility, provide multi-AZ storage resilience with minimal recovery time during failover, and automatically scale read capacity to handle reconciliation reporting during traffic spikes.\n- The solution must minimize administrative overhead.\n\nWhich architecture will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
