    question_en: "A real-estate technology company operates a nationwide property listing platform. The company uses AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts, including dedicated accounts for regional listing services, data analytics workloads, and application backend teams. The company is creating a centralized media repository in an Amazon S3 bucket within a shared services account to store high-resolution property images and architectural blueprints.\n\nApplications running in existing and future member accounts across the organization must be able to read and upload property media directly to this centralized S3 bucket. The company frequently provisions new regional accounts and requires a solution that automatically permits newly created member accounts to access the S3 bucket without requiring manual updates to the bucket configuration or policies.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
