    question_en: "An insurance company is modernizing its claims processing system. When a customer submits an insurance claim, the system must execute several sequential tasks: validating claim documents, analyzing fraud risk, calculating claim payouts, and notifying the claimant. The document validation and payout calculation tasks take less than two minutes each. However, if a claim is flagged for high fraud risk, the workflow must pause and wait for a human claims adjuster's manual review and approval, which can take up to several days. The company wants a serverless solution that provides centralized visibility into workflow states, built-in error handling and retries, and minimizes operational overhead.\n\nWhich architecture meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively with the LEAST operational overhead?",
