    question_en: "A property and casualty insurance company, ApexClaim, operates a claims processing platform on AWS. During severe weather catastrophes, claim submission volume surges unpredictably by more than tenfold within a few minutes. The backend claims evaluation service runs a stateless custom application on Amazon EC2 instances and stores claim data in Amazon DynamoDB and uploaded documents in Amazon S3.\n\nCurrently, the backend instances run on a static fleet of On-Demand EC2 instances behind a single Network Load Balancer. During peak events, users experience latency and timeouts, while during normal periods, the company incurs unnecessary infrastructure costs for idle capacity.\n\nA solutions architect must redesign the compute architecture to be highly available, automatically scale to absorb unpredictable traffic surges within minutes, and minimize infrastructure costs while guaranteeing baseline capacity.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
