    question_en: "A food delivery marketplace company, GourmetDash, hosts its web application on Amazon EC2 instances. The platform experiences predictable traffic peaks during lunch and dinner hours, but also suffers from unpredictable traffic surges caused by flash promotions and unexpected severe weather events. During traffic spikes, instances frequently experience web application process crashes and fail to serve customer HTTP requests, even though the underlying operating system remains running and passes EC2 instance status checks.\n\nA solutions architect must design a highly available architecture that automatically scales compute capacity to maintain an average CPU utilization of 50% during unpredictable surges and automatically replaces instances when the web application process fails.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
