    question_en: "A company is designing the compute infrastructure for a stateless web application hosted on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The application requires a predictable baseline capacity of 6 EC2 instances running 24/7 across multiple Availability Zones. During unexpected traffic surges, demand can rapidly increase to require up to 20 additional instances. The solution must automatically scale to handle unpredictable traffic spikes, ensure high availability, prevent baseline traffic interruptions, and minimize overall compute costs.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
