    question_en: "A SaaS company provides an analytics dashboard platform hosted on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The platform processes sensitive customer telemetry and financial datasets stored in an Amazon S3 bucket.\n\nA solutions architect must design an architecture that meets the following security and compliance requirements:\n- All data in transit between clients, the ALB, and the backend EC2 instances must be encrypted.\n- Datasets stored at rest in the S3 bucket must be encrypted using keys that the company can independently audit, configure access policies for, and automatically rotate on an annual basis.\n- The EC2 instances must securely read and decrypt the datasets from the S3 bucket without storing long-term AWS credentials or static access keys on the instances.\n\nWhich combination of steps will meet these requirements MOST securely?",
