    question_en: "A company is planning to deploy a containerized web application on AWS that will run continuously 24/7 with predictable, steady-state baseline traffic. The application needs to be deployed across multiple Availability Zones for high availability. To maximize compute resource utilization and density, multiple container replicas of the same service must run on each underlying host instance. Traffic must be distributed across the containers using an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Additionally, company compliance policies mandate that custom security monitoring agents must be installed directly on the underlying host operating system.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
