    question_en: "A media streaming company is designing an automated video ingestion and processing pipeline for user-generated content. When creators upload high-resolution video files to an Amazon S3 bucket, the pipeline must immediately extract video metadata and generate preview thumbnails (which takes less than 20 seconds). Afterward, the raw videos must be converted into multiple streaming formats using proprietary encoding software that takes between 35 to 50 minutes per video. The system must gracefully handle unpredictable upload traffic spikes without losing tasks, minimize operational overhead for short tasks, and automatically scale compute capacity based on workload demand.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
