    question_en: "A regional airline operates an online flight booking platform hosted on AWS. The application tier runs on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer, and the data tier uses an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. During seasonal promotional events, frequent user searches for identical flight schedules and routes cause high CPU utilization on the RDS database, leading to slow response times and query timeouts. Additionally, the operations team runs read-heavy analytical queries and booking reports throughout the day, further degrading database performance. A solutions architect must design a highly available architecture that provides sub-millisecond read latency for repetitive flight search queries and isolates analytical reporting traffic from the primary transactional database.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST impact on database performance?",
