    question_en: "A digital healthcare startup, MediSync Health, operates an Electronic Health Record (EHR) web application on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer across multiple Availability Zones. The web tier requires a steady baseline capacity 24/7 to allow clinics to access patient records continuously. In addition, the startup runs automated nightly batch jobs that analyze anonymized medical logs; these batch jobs are stateless, fault-tolerant, and can gracefully recover if interrupted.\n\nThe application backend uses an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. During business hours, intensive read queries from clinic analytical dashboards cause significant CPU utilization spikes on the database. The startup requires 24/7 high availability with automated failover for emergency records access while minimizing overall operational costs.\n\nWhich combination of actions should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
