          "correct": false,
          "reason": "Deploying the critical record-signing nodes in a cluster placement group within a single Availability Zone is incorrect. Cluster placement groups pack instances close together inside a single Availability Zone to achieve high network throughput and ultra-low latency, typically for high-performance computing (HPC) or distributed data processing. However, instances in a cluster placement group share the same underlying rack or infrastructure, offering no physical fault isolation and leaving the validation quorum vulnerable to correlated single-rack or AZ failures."
