    question_en: "A renewable energy company monitors wind turbines and solar farms worldwide. Thousands of IoT edge gateways collect high-frequency sensor readings, package them into compressed log files, and upload them to an Amazon S3 bucket at unpredictable intervals. The company needs an automated solution to extract and parse the telemetry data from each uploaded file and insert the processed records into an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database.\n\nDuring peak operational hours, massive bursts of simultaneous file uploads cause sudden surges in processing concurrency, leading to database connection exhaustion and dropped write transactions. The company requires a resilient ingestion pipeline that automatically processes files upon arrival and prevents database connection overload, while requiring the LEAST operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
