    question_en: "A mobile game studio hosts the backend API for an online multiplayer game on AWS. The application uses AWS Lambda functions to process player requests, which query an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance.\n\nDuring special weekend in-game events, player activity spikes significantly. The engineering team observes two critical bottlenecks:\n- Rapid scaling of concurrent Lambda functions causes database connection exhaustion and frequent connection timeout errors.\n- Read-heavy queries for player profiles, inventory status, and leaderboard standings cause high CPU utilization and severe replication lag on traditional read replicas.\n\nThe studio wants to maintain MySQL compatibility, minimize replication lag for read-heavy operations, and eliminate database connection failures during peak events with minimal application refactoring.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
