    question_en: "A healthcare records startup operates an on-premises data center that hosts its core relational patient database. The company is developing a new cloud-based patient analytics and reporting platform on AWS. The platform must meet the following requirements:\n- Establish a dedicated, private network connection with consistent low latency and predictable bandwidth between the on-premises data center and AWS.\n- Continuously replicate data in near real-time from the on-premises database to AWS with minimal downtime.\n- Deploy a managed database on AWS that provides high availability with automated failover.\n- Offload heavy analytical read queries on AWS so that they do not impact the write performance of the primary database instance.\n\nWhich combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
