    question_en: "A retail chain operates a real-time inventory lookup application that experiences unpredictable traffic spikes during promotional flash sales. During peak shopping events, inventory queries surge dramatically, causing latency issues and occasional service downtime. The application tier is stateless and needs to be migrated to AWS. A solutions architect must design a highly available architecture that automatically scales compute capacity to maintain consistent response times during traffic spikes and automatically detects and replaces failed application instances.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST administrative overhead?",
