    question_en: "A company runs a stateless background processing application on Amazon EC2 instances that consume messages from an Amazon SQS queue. The application requires a minimum baseline of 4 instances running 24/7 to maintain continuous processing without interruption. During peak periods, message volume surges unpredictably, requiring up to 20 instances. Processing tasks above the baseline capacity can tolerate worker interruptions. The company needs to implement an automated scaling solution that maintains high availability and meets these requirements with the lowest possible cost.\n\nWhich solution should a solutions architect recommend?",
