    question_en: "A company runs a multi-tier web application on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The application stores structured data in an Amazon RDS database and unstructured files in an Amazon S3 bucket. A security audit requires the company to meet the following requirements:\n\n- All data in transit must be encrypted end-to-end, including traffic between clients and the ALB as well as between the ALB and the backend EC2 instances.\n- All data at rest in Amazon RDS and Amazon S3 must be encrypted.\n- The security team must have full control over key access policies, monitor key usage via AWS CloudTrail, and enable automatic key rotation.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
