    question_en: "An insurance company is developing a new claims processing system for policyholders and adjusters to submit damage claims via mobile and web applications. The volume of claim submissions is highly variable, experiencing sharp spikes during severe storm events and virtually zero activity during overnight hours.\n\nThe company requires a secure RESTful API endpoint that:\n- Authenticates external users and applies rate limiting to prevent API abuse during sudden traffic surges.\n- Parses and validates claim submission payloads and stores the claim records in a NoSQL database.\n- Operates with minimal operational overhead and eliminates costs associated with idle server capacity.\n\nWhich architecture should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?",
