    question_en: "An organization ingests large telemetry archive files ranging from 20 GB to 80 GB into an Amazon S3 bucket using multipart uploads. Due to occasional network timeouts during uploads, incomplete multipart uploads remain in the bucket and incur ongoing storage charges.\n\nThe uploaded files are accessed frequently during the first 30 days for data validation and reporting. After 30 days, the files are rarely accessed but must be retained for 7 years to meet compliance mandates. An audit retrieval time of up to 12 hours is acceptable for any archived files.\n\nA solutions architect must recommend a solution that removes incomplete multipart uploads and minimizes long-term storage costs with the LEAST operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
