    question_en: "A regional airline company, AeroVanguard, operates an online flight booking platform. The platform experiences unpredictable and massive surges in read traffic during seasonal promotional fare sales. The web and booking application tier runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The backend database is currently hosted on an Amazon RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ DB instance. During promotional sales, the primary database instance suffers from high CPU utilization, severe read latency, and connection exhaustion caused by rapid compute scaling. The airline needs a highly available, scalable architecture that can automatically handle read traffic bursts with minimal replication lag, prevent database connection overload, and ensure resilient compute capacity across multiple Availability Zones with the least operational overhead.\n\nWhich architecture should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?",
