    question_en: "A company hosts a memory-intensive batch processing workload on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances managed by an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer. The application frequently experiences performance bottlenecks and out-of-memory errors during peak periods, while CPU utilization remains well below 35%. The Auto Scaling group is currently configured to scale based on default Amazon CloudWatch CPU utilization metrics, which fails to trigger scale-out events when memory is exhausted. A solutions architect must design an automated scaling solution based on memory utilization while adhering to security best practices for credential management.\n\nWhich solution should the solutions architect implement to meet these requirements?",
