    question_en: "PrecisionGear Industrial operates a smart manufacturing facility where legacy IoT sensor logging systems collect high-frequency vibration and temperature telemetry from CNC milling machines. The on-premises systems only support standard NFS file share protocols and have limited local disk capacity. However, factory floor engineers require immediate, low-latency access to the most recent 24 hours of telemetry files for local equipment health monitoring. Additionally, the company must run a daily machine learning anomaly detection and aggregation workload in the cloud on the entire historical dataset. The daily batch workload is stateless, fault-tolerant, can recover from compute interruptions, and must run at the lowest possible compute cost while adhering to AWS security best practices.\n\nWhich combination of services and architectures best meets these requirements?",
