    question_en: "An insurance company, SureShield Life, hosts a digital claims processing application on AWS. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The system requires a constant baseline capacity of 10 EC2 instances running 24/7 to process routine claims. During severe weather events and regional filing deadlines, incoming claims traffic surges unpredictably, requiring up to 40 additional instances. The claims processing tasks are stateless and fault-tolerant, allowing interrupted tasks to be safely retried.\n\nA solutions architect must design a highly available architecture that handles these unpredictable traffic surges while minimizing overall compute costs.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
